# Pylivetrader EMA12/26 MACD State

## Source
- Source: [[sources/github-topic-algorithmic-trading-python]]
- Topic URL: https://github.com/topics/algorithmic-trading?l=python
- Repository: https://github.com/alpacahq/pylivetrader
- Primary file: https://github.com/alpacahq/pylivetrader/blob/master/examples/MACD/macd_example.py
- Author / institution: Alpaca / `alpacahq`.
- Source location: `examples/MACD/macd_example.py`.

## Mechanics

### Entry
- Evaluate once per completed M15 bar after warmup.
- Compute EMA(12) and EMA(26) from close.
- Define MACD as `EMA(12) - EMA(26)`.
- Enter long when MACD is greater than zero.

### Exit
- Close long when MACD is less than zero.
- If MACD is exactly zero, hold current state.

### Stop Loss
- Source does not define a protective stop.
- P2 baseline: `2.0 * ATR(14)` hard stop from entry.

### Position Sizing
- P2 baseline: `RISK_FIXED = 1000`.
- Live: `RISK_PERCENT = 0.25`.
- One open position per symbol/magic.

### Additional Filters
- Minimum warmup: 100 M15 bars.
- Optional P3 gate: require MACD to cross zero this bar rather than merely remain positive.
- Friday close flatten uses V5 framework defaults.

## Concepts
- [[concepts/macd-zero-line]] - source trades long while the fast EMA is above the slow EMA, expressed as a positive EMA spread.

